{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01132",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.19,
      "end_seconds": 4.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Hi there, the chair's free, sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.54,
      "end_seconds": 9.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Afternoon, um, is this seat fine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.7,
      "end_seconds": 16.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Is the form from the front desk all filled in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.86,
      "end_seconds": 24.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Well, um, I think so, I handed it in at the counter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.66,
      "end_seconds": 30.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Right, what would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.25,
      "end_seconds": 41.47,
      "duration_seconds": 9.22,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, it's my face drooping on the right side. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.52,
      "end_seconds": 43.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.08,
      "end_seconds": 59.67,
      "duration_seconds": 14.59,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, around about four days... no wait, it's more like two days. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.33,
      "end_seconds": 64.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.44,
      "end_seconds": 68.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.87,
      "end_seconds": 72.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.55,
      "end_seconds": 94.78,
      "duration_seconds": 20.23,
      "text": "Okay, so it usually comes with food tasting odd. The food tasting odd? That's been for about a month. Okay, so about food tasting odd, mostly severe. And a watery eye as well, since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.68,
      "end_seconds": 103.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Have you had your face drooping on the right side before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.32,
      "end_seconds": 112.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "I had a similar thing a couple of years ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.66,
      "end_seconds": 119.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "A few quick ones: slurred speech or rash around the ear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.24,
      "end_seconds": 124.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.05,
      "end_seconds": 128.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "A few quick ones: headache or hearing changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.86,
      "end_seconds": 133.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "No, no headache or hearing changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.56,
      "end_seconds": 137.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.58,
      "end_seconds": 140.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.64,
      "end_seconds": 144.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.31,
      "end_seconds": 147.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.01,
      "end_seconds": 151.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.19,
      "end_seconds": 158.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Okay, so I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.3,
      "end_seconds": 175.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.51,
      "end_seconds": 182.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Okay, so no, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.05,
      "end_seconds": 186.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.04,
      "end_seconds": 201.81,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop. I retired from the post office two years ago. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.18,
      "end_seconds": 205.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.21,
      "end_seconds": 211.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "I have diabetes. I've been putting this off for weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.53,
      "end_seconds": 227.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Alright, tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.32,
      "end_seconds": 236.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "Metformin. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.08,
      "end_seconds": 241.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.9,
      "end_seconds": 249.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.37,
      "end_seconds": 272.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature is 36.7 degrees, BP is 124 over 74, pulse 73, respiratory rate 15."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.8,
      "end_seconds": 276.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.86,
      "end_seconds": 280.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Yes, you know, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.53,
      "end_seconds": 283.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.48,
      "end_seconds": 308.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "You can't wrinkle the right forehead or puff out the right cheek."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.13,
      "end_seconds": 310.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.48,
      "end_seconds": 327.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Left side of the face moves normally, and arm and leg strength is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.26,
      "end_seconds": 333.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.82,
      "end_seconds": 363.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.94,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, the most likely explanation is a Bell's palsy pattern. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 364.54,
      "end_seconds": 366.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.52,
      "end_seconds": 389.45,
      "duration_seconds": 21.93,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a Bell's palsy pattern, and we'll know more once the blood sugar testing is back. Blood sugar testing is what I'd like next, for facial palsy. What I'm giving you is prednisolone, 50 milligrams, once a day, for seven days. That's for facial weakness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.25,
      "end_seconds": 392.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "That's simple enough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.53,
      "end_seconds": 410.09,
      "duration_seconds": 15.56,
      "text": "Use lubricating drops through the day and tape the eye shut at night. The thing that would worry me is if the weakness spreads to your arm or leg, or your speech changes. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.78,
      "end_seconds": 416.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Yes, you know, I'll bear that in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 418.5,
      "end_seconds": 424.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "See me again in a week. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.28,
      "end_seconds": 430.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Okay, um, so I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.93,
      "end_seconds": 433.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}